      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "LoRA reference loop\n\n1. Load Prompt List: click \"upload yaml\" and pick custom_nodes/personal-utils/lora_dataset_prompts.yaml.\n2. Reference Picker: click \"Upload photos\" and pick your reference photos, they go to input/<Reference Analyzer's folder>.\n3. Click \"Analyze\" on the Reference Picker. It runs only the Reference Analyzer, which stays muted so Run never analyzes again.\n4. Open \"Anchors\", click 3-5 photos that clearly show the subject alone, then Analyze again. The subject is found in every other photo by face, other people count against a photo.\n5. Go through the prompts and click photos to pick or unpick them. Hover a photo for its score breakdown, \"Weights\" changes how much each part counts.\n6. Pick the Qwen Image 2.1 model files in the Models group and Run. Each prompt is saved to output/lora_dataset as <id>_0001.png.\n7. Untick prompts in the picker's list to leave them out. Run only makes the ticked prompts with no image in output/lora_dataset yet (Pending Prompts).\n8. Open \"Results\" to approve or reject the images. Rejected ones move to output/lora_dataset/rejected and are made again on the next Run.\n\nCaptions are in the YAML (\"caption\"), replace TRIGGER and [HAIR COLOR] before training."
      ]
    },
